# Virtual environments. Without a trailing slash, so each pattern also matches
# a symbolic link of that name: a worktree that borrows another checkout's
# environment links it in, and `dir/` matches only a real directory, so a
# `git add -A` there would commit the link and the home path it points at.
venv
env/
.env
.env/
.venv
# The viewer's packages, linked the same way. viewer/.gitignore's
# `node_modules/` covers only the real directory.
node_modules

