# The YAML recipe level 5 step 04 writes beside itself. Run from a copy the
# reader made, that file is the step's own output and belongs next to the
# model; run in place from a checkout, it is the same output landing in the
# package tree. Ignored rather than redirected, because moving it would take
# the lesson -- the recipe sits beside the model it is a recipe for -- with it.
bindings/python/gaspatchio/tutorials/**/plan.yaml

# Local dogfooding / stress scratch dirs (probes & generated outputs, never shipped)
/bindings/python/tests/scratch/gsp*/
/evals/benchmarks/aggregated_results/
/evals/benchmarks/batch_search_results/

# Emission-graph performance probe: the synthesized 100k-policy fixture and
# the machine-local reference JSON reports it produces are generated
# artifacts, not source — only the harness and synthesizer scripts are
# tracked (tests/probe/*.py).
/bindings/python/tests/probe/fixtures/
/bindings/python/tests/probe/reference/*.json

# Artifact of the repository-root workspace boundary in ./pyproject.toml: any uv command
# run from the repository root writes an empty 3-line lockfile here. It is meaningless —
# the real lockfile is bindings/python/uv.lock, tracked, below.
/uv.lock

# uv lockfile IS tracked (bindings/python/uv.lock) — deliberately, see GSP issue #33.
# Resolving dev dependencies fresh on every CI run made unrelated PRs fail: ruff floated
# to 0.16.0 on 2026-07-25 and its changed I001 behaviour broke ~70 docstring-example tests
# on a PR that touched none of them. CI installs with `uv sync --locked`, so a PR's result
# depends only on its own diff. Distribution is still via the built wheel, whose deps come
# from pyproject.toml — consumers never see this file.
# To take a new dependency version: run `uv lock` and commit the result as part of the PR.

# What the Measurement Ratchets steps leave behind. Each step redirects its
# tool's output to a file beside the package and reads the count back out of
# it, so a contributor reproducing a step at a keyboard -- which is the whole
# design of those steps -- leaves the same four files in the working tree. The
# steps write them here rather than somewhere already ignored precisely so
# that the keyboard command and the CI command stay identical.
/bindings/python/ruff.json
/bindings/python/mypy.txt
/bindings/python/pyright.json
/bindings/python/pyright.err
